# Knight

## Lore

The knights of Rifts Earth have little in common with the landed nobility of old. They are closer to musketeers: men and women, human and D-Bee, trained to fight and bound by a shared devotion to life, freedom, country and the code of chivalry. At least half cannot read or write, and few have any tie to royalty or wealth. They are idealists who wander a Europe under siege by monsters, righting wrongs, protecting the weak and freeing the oppressed.

A knight learns the way from other knights: as an apprentice under an older knight, as a squire tending a master''s horse and gear, at a school run by a kingdom or an order, or by teaching themselves from stories and practice. Most wear environmental hard suits styled after medieval plate, often with plumed hats, high boots, gauntlets and bright capes. Thirty years ago there were almost no knights outside the British Isles; the fame of the Knights of Camelot has made them common everywhere, which the New German Republic watches with some unease. Black knights, who have abandoned the code, are despised by true knights.

## GM Notes

Weapons beyond the sheet: a sidearm and an energy rifle of choice. Knights vary widely; some favour magic or ancient weapons (usually high-tech versions such as vibro-blades, neuro-maces and tech-arrows), some purely modern arms and implants, most a mix. Some are partial or full conversion borgs.

Armor: an M.D.C. environmental hard suit in the style of medieval plate, 60 to 100 M.D.C., fair to poor mobility, -10% to -20% to prowl, 17 to 25 pounds (7.7 to 11.3 kg), often with a detachable jet pack. Power armor may be used instead.

Mount: a horse, bionic horse, robot horse, hover cycle, motorcycle, A.T.V. or jet pack; 15% ride an exotic animal such as a pegasus, unicorn, dragondactyl or gryphon (-10% to Horsemanship on these).

Money: 1D6x1000 credits plus 3D6x100 credits'' worth of gems, precious metals or artifacts.

Cybernetics: the player may select two cybernetic (not bionic) implants at first level; any more must be bought.

Optional background (roll d100): 01-10 illegitimate child of a knight, king or noble; 11-20 son of nobility; 21-30 child of a farmer or laborer; 31-40 child of a career soldier; 41-50 child of a vagabond family; 51-60 a D-Bee seeking to rise above disdain; 61-70 rich or poor (50/50), family destroyed by supernatural monsters, seeking revenge; 71-80 a D-Bee warrior defending other non-humans; 81-90 child of a wilderness scout or other fighting class; 91-00 child of a knight following family tradition.
', 'published', 'data-script'
